# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7 (R3: a dynamic's update event fires at n with the value after n) and ch. 8 (`<-` binds the widget's result, here the clause's hold): each click writes the hold behind `$r`, and `!Updated $r` fires in that tick.
test a_clause_widgets_result_is_heard

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    1: Ui.Label(text="1 heard 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="2 heard 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="3 heard 2")
